    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p>A sailor who died centuries ago near the isle of Solstice, his body possessed by the spirit of one of Auril's dead frost druids. He appears as a tanned, dark-haired man in his thirties \u2014 until he dies, when his true age catches up to him instantly.</p>\n<p>Sephek is not lucid. He does not negotiate, explain himself, or respond to reason. He is a mechanism, not a person \u2014 the enforcement of a single belief: <strong>once chosen for sacrifice, there is no escape.</strong> When someone selected for sacrifice is rescued or flees, Sephek finds them and finishes what Auril \"already claimed.\" Anyone who helps them escape dies too.</p>\n<p><strong>DM \u2014 Encounter context:</strong> Sephek stalks the party to Ramshackle in Lonelywood after they interfered with a sacrifice at the Twenty Stones of Thruun (the unnamed woman Savaa Rubyeye was sacrificing). He isolates and attacks whoever is easiest to catch alone \u2014 ambush, not a fair fight. Designed as a tough SOLO fight against one party member for 2-3 rounds before others can wake and reach the room. Once the rest of the party arrives, this should not be a prolonged grind \u2014 he's meant to be beaten once backup shows up, not a full-party boss fight.</p>\n<p><strong>During combat, if fighting the party (not just his isolated target), he only repeats:</strong> <em>\"She was chosen. You interfered. She was chosen. You interfered.\"</em> He says nothing else. He does not explain, threaten, or monologue beyond this.</p>\n<p><strong>On death:</strong> A translucent, frost-blue spirit exits his body through his mouth and eyes, drifting up and away into the night sky. His corpse instantly ages \u2014 desiccates, hollows, and cracks like something that has been dead for centuries, because it has.</p>"
      },
